# oracle: fix setforce 0 0 0 on an anchor group with bonds (bond_style harmonic, atom_style bond), fix addforce on the far end,
# fix viscous, a cut-down examples/bpm/plasticity cantilever (in.bpm.plasticity, bpm/spring/plastic replaced by harmonic).
# Shrink-wrapped boundaries: the anchored atoms drift ballistically and bonds stay short of any periodic image; with boundary p
# in x the same system diverges from native once an anchored atom crosses the x boundary (see w60fix_bond_image for the bond image rule).
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-5 abs=1e-9
units lj
newton on off
dimension 3
boundary s s s
atom_style bond
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 0.0 1.0 1.0
comm_modify vel yes cutoff 2.6
lattice fcc 1.41
region box block 0 12 -1 9 -5 5 units box
create_box 1 box bond/types 1 extra/bond/per/atom 20
mass * 1.0
region cantilever block 3.0 9.0 0 8 -2.5 2.5 units box
create_atoms 1 region cantilever
velocity all create 0.1 345910 loop geom
pair_style lj/cut 1.0
pair_coeff * * 0.0 1.0
fix 1 all nve
compute zmin1 all reduce min z
region anchor block 3.0 3.6 EDGE EDGE EDGE EDGE units box
group anchor region anchor
fix 5 anchor setforce 0.0 0.0 0.0
thermo_style custom step ke pe c_zmin1 f_5[1] f_5[2] f_5[3]
thermo_modify format float %.15g norm no
thermo 20
timestep 0.1
run 60
neighbor 1.0 bin
create_bonds many all all 1 0.0 1.5
neighbor 0.3 bin
special_bonds lj 0.0 1.0 1.0 coul 1.0 1.0 1.0
bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff 1 1.0 1.0
region load block EDGE EDGE 7.0 EDGE EDGE EDGE units box
group load region load
variable fload equal ramp(0.0,-0.0005)
fix 3 load addforce 0.0 0.0 v_fload
thermo 1
fix 4 all viscous 0.0016
run 200
unfix 3
fix 3 load addforce 0.0 0.0 -0.0005
run 200
